WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:04.684
Convolutional neural networks lean heavily on color
to recognize objects,

00:00:04.764 --> 00:00:08.925
but real-world data rarely contains every color a
class can take.

00:00:09.005 --> 00:00:13.884
When a model trained mostly on red cars sees a blue
one, accuracy collapses.

00:00:13.964 --> 00:00:16.299
The classic remedy, color invariance,

00:00:16.379 --> 00:00:19.496
sidesteps the problem by removing color entirely,

00:00:19.576 --> 00:00:22.563
but that throws away a genuinely useful signal.

00:00:22.643 --> 00:00:28.371
The paper frames the real challenge as keeping
color information while still generalizing

00:00:28.451 --> 00:00:31.960
across colors that were rare or absent during training.
